  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Thursday)\nIssued at 1243 AM CDT Fri Jun 26 2026\n\nThe forecast remains benign through at least the middle of next\nweek. Upper level ridge will remain the primary influence over \nour day to day weather through the next 7 days. By early next week\nthe center of the ridge axis shifts to the east of our area in \nresponse to a deepening upper level trough over the western U.S. \nNevertheless, we will maintain a generally hot and dry forecast. \nWe may be close to heat advisory criteria this weekend across \nportions of the Big Country where temperatures may reach 104-106 \ndegrees. For the rest of west central Texas highs will climb into \nthe upper 90s to near 103 degrees Saturday though Monday. The \nstatus quo will continue through the middle of of next week, with \nhighs on Tuesday and Wednesday in the mid 90s to near 102 degrees.",
